{
  "_system": [
    "ONE DRAWING PER MODULE, AUTHORED. Same hand and same 48-unit grid as the",
    "specimen art, with flat colour added.",
    "",
    "A path is either a bare string (stroke only) or a [d, role] pair. No role",
    "names a colour: fill, deep and tint resolve against the module's own world",
    "palette, so a drawing inherits its hue and dark mode for nothing and cannot",
    "introduce a colour the generator never gated. hatch is a lighter stroke.",
    "",
    "THE RULE THAT MAKES THEM READ AS DRAWINGS. The first version was eight to",
    "twelve geometric paths and read as an icon set. The ones that worked — the",
    "leaf, the shield, the beetle — all had the same thing: an ORGANIC FILLED",
    "SILHOUETTE with structure inside it. So every drawing now has, in order:",
    "  1. two or three filled shapes, the largest carrying the world's mid tone",
    "  2. the same shapes again as outline, so the line work sits on the colour",
    "  3. six to twelve strokes of internal structure",
    "  4. three to six hatch strokes, always on the lower right, so one light",
    "     direction runs through all twenty-five",
    "Twenty to thirty-two paths. Forty is the build's runaway guard, not a target.",
    "",
    "RULES, checked by tools/build.mjs: 48x48 grid, safe area 4..44, absolute",
    "commands only, fills before line work, at least one colour, at most 40 paths.",
    "",
    "Draw the module's IDEA, never its title. (D82, D83)"
  ],
